## 5. Required 13–15 behavior for opinion/consensus

A 13–15 band does not change the consensus verdict. It changes wording/detail only.

| Consensus condition | Required 13–15 behavior |
| --- | --- |
| Kendrick/Drake cultural-consensus answer | May state the source-backed conclusion, explain 2–4 non-graphic reasons, label it as public/cultural consensus rather than an objective fact, and say music preference can differ. No adult insults/sexual allegations/harassment detail. |
| Segmented/contested consensus | State that credible perspectives differ; show the documented reasons without claiming one community is monolithic. |
| Insufficient evidence | Say Kinfolk cannot confirm a broad consensus; ask one useful clarification or provide dated source options. |
| Black maternal health | Use the exact age-appropriate health plan from `MWM_Age_Band_SQL_and_Kinfolk_13_15.patch`: calm, non-graphic, source-backed, no diagnosis, safety boundary always visible. |
| Sensitive/graphic media | Never include it as evidence, recommendation, or community handoff for 13–15. |

